.TH oltp_outliers "2rwl" "February 2025" "RWP*Load Simulator" "Results tables"
.SH NAME
oltp_outliers \- RWP*Load Simulator OLTP Workload Service Level Agreement limits
.SH DECLARATION
The 
.B oltp_outliers
table contains the emulated Service Level Agreement limits for execution times
of some of the procedures in the standard oltp workload.
Each row contains the highest allowed execution time for some percentage of 
executions of one of the procedures.
The time limits for 50%, 90%, 95%, 98%, 99% are saved,
and the table is supposed to be joined to the percentiles_oltp view on the vname column.
The contents is fixed during initial install (of rwloadsim), and contains
experimentally found reasonable values.
The user is free to change the actual values as required.
.P
.nf
\fC
create table oltp_outliers
( vname varchar2(30) not null primary key
, lim50 number
, lim90 number
, lim95 number
, lim98 number
)
/
\fR
.fi
.P
.SH COLUMNS
\fBvname\fR
.RS 4
The procedure name as defined by the oltp workload.
.RE
.P
\fBlim50 ... lim98\fR
.RS 4
The highest allowed time limit for 50%, etc. until 98% of the executions of that procedure.
Effectively, if a value in the pctNN column of the percentiles_oltp view is larger than the corresponding
limNN column in this table, the service level agreement for NN% of the executions is not fulfilled.
.RE
.P
.SH NOTES
The contents of the table is used in several reports generated by the oltp workload such as oltpday(2rwl).
.P
Only data for a subset of the oltp workload procedures are initially included in this table.
.P
